      "text": "Spring Grove was founded in the 1800s by Quaker pioneer Isaac Evans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://springgroveindiana.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Evans’ 1864 home on Chester Boulevard now serves as the town hall and a popular event venue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://springgroveindiana.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town is enveloped by Richmond, which annexed its northern areas beyond the I‑70 interchange many years ago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://springgroveindiana.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Thistlethwaite Falls, a Whitewater River tributary, sits on Spring Grove’s western border and draws visitors all seasons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://springgroveindiana.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Quaker Hill Conference Center, built in 1855 by Evans, remains a versatile community facility.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://springgroveindiana.com/about/"
    },
    {
